      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"phantaskippy\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/phantaskippy/48/1897_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> phantaskippy:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>the fabric isn't going to hold up under beatings and slober and all the things a primary stuffed companion has to survive with newborns.I wouldn't go with Mr. Chomps as a primary companion, not one to sleep with or drag around and chew on. &nbsp;It's not really unsafe or fragile, just not newborn -toddler friendly.&nbsp;</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Plus, Mr. Chomps is not optimized for flight.</p>",
